# ll-federation chunked-upload wire fixture, protocol v3.
#
# Vendored byte-for-byte by BOTH learning-loop (native/crates/ll-search) and
# sync-hub. Neither repo can see the other, so the pinned fixture-sha256 in
# each repo's test is the contract: a wire change that is not made on both
# sides reddens its own side instead of silently breaking an upload.
#
# body      = (0..2500).map(|i| (i % 251) as u8)
# chunking  = 1000 bytes, so three frames of 1000/1000/500
# frame     = seq:u32be | total:u32be | body_size:u32be | sha256(body) | body
#
# Values below are lowercase hex. Regenerate only when the wire format
# itself changes, and update the pinned sha256 in both repos in the same
# change.

body-sha256 a75c5b146f3ad9d2e6e54652e71eb6a1d206ffb1348bed2c2f43b51ddaac0f88
chunks 3
chunk 0 
chunk 1 
chunk 2 
